o.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. También revisar si en diciembre se adjudicaron otros contratos cerca del límite y si hubo repeticiones de adjudicatarios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 37 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 4.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 9.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.2 to 16.8. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. Contract [1], for 14,754 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [2], for 14,943.40 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove misconduct. Prices might be standard, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check contract dates and amounts for consistency. Review if multiple contracts cover the same need. Look at award patterns across different months to see if there's a systemic trend.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["4iHJzUPJ1jZeKgd8LfVV9g%3D%3D","YsscTTA7U4k%2Bk2oCbDosIw%3D%3D","NC%2FvlzD%2B7aYeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}